WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:04.910
Tommy and his new friends got a free flight from the Royal Knights to Beanstalk Village.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.570
So Takuya and the gang wormed their way onto a Trailmon and were soon in hot pursuit.

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.750
Turns out Crusadermon and Dinosmon heard about the key to the village

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:15.370
and made the Mami-mon miserable trying to find it.

00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:19.170
When Tommy and Koji rolled into town, the unity evolved and the battle began.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:23.910
Things looked grim for our heroes, so Elder Mami-mon told the regal rats where the key was.

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:28.610
Luckily, everybody got out of town just in time, and Katsuharu and his buds left for home.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:29.970
But we're not through with the Royal...

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.000
past

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:40.140
Headphones

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:41.960
To reclaim

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:43.480
It's a word.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.610
There are cells.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:47.940
Trust in you.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:36.060
We'll be right back.

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:41.800
We all got home safely.

00:01:42.350 --> 00:01:43.510
I'm sure they're fine.

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.430
Don't worry, Tommy. I'm sure Wyrm wouldn't let anything happen to them.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:50.130
It's pretty empty out there. There's hardly anything left to save.

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:52.230
We've got ourselves a royal problem.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.030
What are we gonna do about those guys? We can't beat them.

00:01:55.250 --> 00:01:55.870
I know.

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:57.670
Hey, how can you even say that?

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:00.000
We have to find a way to beat them!

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.200
them.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.080
No matter what.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:06.110
In case you're interested, the village of Beginnings should be just up ahead.

00:02:06.310 --> 00:02:07.410
Well, the name's interesting.

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:07.930
Huh?

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:11.020
It's the place where all Digimon are born!

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:11.600
Really?

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.360
Can a Purified Digi-Egg go there to start over?

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.440
Very good question, Zoe, but with all the scanning going on lately,

00:02:17.480 --> 00:02:19.280
I'm just hoping the village is still there.

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:20.000
Woo!

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.180
lot steeper than I remember. I think I can, I think I can, blah, blah.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.160
Get out and get lost!

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:41.800
What a beautiful place to be born!

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.180
Indeed, it's the only place for Digimon.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:47.800
The safety of this village and everything in it

00:02:47.800 --> 00:02:49.580
is critical to our very existence.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:53.520
I don't know about you guys, but I'm pretty egg-cited to be here!

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:55.660
Egg-cited? Egg-salad!

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:56.660
Oh, cool!

00:02:57.140 --> 00:02:58.300
Wow, I can't believe it!

00:02:58.570 --> 00:02:59.910
They're even prettier up close!

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.720
The village is full of them.

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.090
Extraordinary and educational!

00:03:05.050 --> 00:03:05.810
I'll stop that.

00:03:10.190 --> 00:03:12.220
Who's there?

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:14.210
What?

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.480
Step away from the egg right now, intruder.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:21.310
One Mon, feathered yet fierce.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.610
This Digimon's beauty is only rivaled by her protective instincts.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:28.210
The feathers will definitely start flying if you try to mess with this mama.

00:03:31.750 --> 00:03:31.990
Bye.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.440
Yeah, I'm sorry.

00:03:33.900 --> 00:03:35.800
In that case, I bid you loving welcome.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.620
I am Swanmon, the caretaker and protector of the Village of Beginnings.

00:03:41.900 --> 00:03:42.420
Wow!

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:48.340
I make sure they receive water and nutrients every day.

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.100
They must be carefully nurtured.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.820
These eggs are the precious treasures of the digital world.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.500
But there's so many. How do you take care of them all?

00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:59.480
It is a very difficult job and getting much more so every day.

00:04:09.700 --> 00:04:18.520
It always seems to move me when I see a new life beginning.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:20.860
Makes me reminisce about my pet-a-mom.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:27.580
My baby!

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.970
I'll never forget the first time he called me-

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:30.900
Papamom!

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:32.610
Papamom!

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.520
I love you, baby!

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:37.510
What's happening?

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.540
It's the four evil warriors.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:42.500
Their data seems to be reacting for some reason.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.800
Zoe, remember the question you asked me?

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:47.970
The eggs of the evil legendary warriors you scanned

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.030
must have been sent back here to start over.

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.460
So does that mean they'll be reborn someday?

00:04:52.700 --> 00:04:53.940
After all that work?

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.480
Wait, when we scan them, we purify them, right?

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.060
Plus, Cherubimon's gone, so this time when they're reborn,

00:04:59.180 --> 00:04:59.980
there's no way they'll be...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:02.140
You're right. Excuse me.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:02.860
Huh?

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:06.530
Sorry to interrupt, but it's time to feed this little one and get him to bed,

00:05:06.670 --> 00:05:08.710
and I'm sure the others are quite hungry by now.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:12.170
The others? How many others are there? Would you like some help?

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:16.490
Oh, I couldn't ask you to do that, but you're welcome to come in and see them if you like.

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:17.480
This way.

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.890
Are these babies by yourself?

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.540
Yes, normally it's only for a day or so, then the Trailmon take them to their families.

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.940
But the Trailmon seem to have stopped coming lately.

00:05:39.470 --> 00:05:40.470
Why would they stop?

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.410
I heard the Beanstalk Village disappeared recently.

00:05:43.770 --> 00:05:45.810
The whole digital world seems to be under attack,

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.770
and the Trailmon are frightened and have decided to hide in their tunnels.

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.420
Trailmon act more like babies than babies!

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:54.490
Anyway, whatever the reason is, I'm here by myself.

00:05:54.810 --> 00:05:56.790
And you guys need some milk, don't you?

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.720
Swanmon, let me help!

00:05:58.800 --> 00:05:59.640
I love babies!

00:05:59.760 --> 00:05:59.880
Yeah!

00:06:00.350 --> 00:06:08.540
I've got plenty of experience very well, but it's not going to be easy. Now don't let them drink too fast

00:06:08.540 --> 00:06:11.400
They'll get very cranky if they get bubbles in their tummies

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:16.580
I've had to face a lot of challenges in the digital world, but this is what I never imagined myself doing

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.890
Baby, it's good stuff. Just take the bottle

00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:29.840
Wow, doesn't it feel like we're a mom and dad feeding our baby together

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:31.100
Huh?

00:06:31.530 --> 00:06:31.750
No.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:35.690
I guess she's just not comfortable with her love for me yet.

00:06:36.060 --> 00:06:37.220
Like you love me, huh?

00:06:39.110 --> 00:06:40.350
Now that's comfortable.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:42.800
Man, they're amazing, aren't they?

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.740
I wonder if this is how we were fed when you and I were little babies.

00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:46.410
Huh?

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:52.560
Forgetting that the two of us were together when we were born.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:53.800
There you go.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:58.200
I promise there's enough for Buddy.

00:06:58.400 --> 00:06:59.980
That is, if you can behave yourself...

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:07.550
Thank you, but I did learn a lot about babies from you.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.260
They're finally asleep, you everyone.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.060
I couldn't have done it without all your help.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:16.060
We did it, huh?

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.050
I don't know how you do this alone.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:21.980
If you'd like a job here, I'd be happy to hire you.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.060
Now who wants some tea?

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:26.460
So tell me, is it true that you've inherited

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:28.680
the spirits of the great legendary warriors?

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:29.860
You bet your boot?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.320
Hey, aren't you gonna put him down so you can eat?

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:35.330
I would, but he cries every time I do.

00:07:35.780 --> 00:07:37.020
That's because you spoiled him.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:38.900
Guess the little booger thinks you're his mom or something.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:42.120
Wish my mom were here to spoil me.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:49.280
Everybody, is something wrong with the food?

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.940
Oh no, am I gonna be sick again?

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.080
You really know how to kill the mood.

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:56.280
You know what? This was right.

00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.050
I'm glad I decided not to go home.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:04.460
I'm a big kid now being here is a very important job. You're right about that

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:08.680
I mean after all how many kids can say that they're half Digimon? That is pretty cool

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:14.040
I remember how weird it felt the first time my spirit evolved. Now it just seems normal

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:18.680
I can't even imagine not being able to become a Digimon anymore. I am Beetlemon

00:08:18.680 --> 00:08:23.980
Yeah, it's definitely made me a lot stronger. I used to be afraid of everything

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:29.980
You know what's even better? We have two birthdays we can celebrate one when we were born

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.640
and one when we became Digimon.

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:34.420
Yeah, I know my life will never be the same.

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:39.520
That's why we have to stick together

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.860
and do everything we can to save the digital world.

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.690
This is our home too, and I'm proud to be a Digimon!

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:45.820
Me too!

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:47.910
Thank you all very much.

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:51.030
Well, gang, what do you say we go try to talk some sense

00:08:51.030 --> 00:08:54.030
into those silly Trailmon and see about getting those babies home?

00:08:54.230 --> 00:08:55.110
That would be wonderful.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:16.480
of beginnings. Looks like a tasty birthday cake. It is quite beautiful. Lucemon will be pleased.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:24.240
It's a shame we have to scan it. I can't believe the Trailmon are wussing out like this.

00:09:24.860 --> 00:09:29.860
I suppose even giant Digimon like them have the right to be afraid once in a while. I think it's a lot

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:33.150
in here than outside. Man, those guys are weird.

00:09:33.710 --> 00:09:34.110
Jinx!

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:37.130
Who is that?

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:39.860
We're looking for the Trailmon.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.760
That's just...

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:46.900
You have to take the babies home.

00:09:47.080 --> 00:09:49.260
There's just too many. Swanmon is overwhelmed.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:51.000
You don't get it, pal, do you?

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.660
We don't want to get hurt.

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:53.480
Me too.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:56.420
But if you guys stop running, the bad guys win,

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:57.560
and what about the babies?

00:09:57.780 --> 00:09:59.780
What about them, huh? What about them?

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.500
Yeah, babies are a lot more resilient than we are.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.060
Sorry, Kinder, but it's just too dangerous.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:06.200
I'll be the same!

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.120
Welcome back, that was fast.

00:10:10.390 --> 00:10:11.430
So, how did it go?

00:10:12.150 --> 00:10:15.690
By decree of Lord Lucemon, we shall now scan this village.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:18.790
Are you two out of your minds? This is the village of beginnings!

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.650
Well, for every beginning, there must be an end.

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.610
We are here to facilitate that.

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:39.900
Cowards! Guess we'll have to Spirit Evolve and take the babies ourselves!

00:10:42.630 --> 00:10:45.800
I'm sorry, Swanmon. The Trailmon just wouldn't cooperate.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:47.550
Run! Hurry!

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.660
Swanmon, what's wrong?

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:59.840
It's here and just in time. The party's about to begin.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:02.100
Hope you like scrambled eggs.

00:11:02.320 --> 00:11:04.220
Do you have any idea of what you're doing?

00:11:04.420 --> 00:11:05.620
This place is sacred.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:08.640
If you harm anything here, you'll upset the balance of all Digimon life.

00:11:08.880 --> 00:11:09.880
Don't you understand?

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:11.660
This is where Digimon are born.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:12.440
Not anymore.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:15.660
Clones will be easier for Lord Lucimon to control.

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:18.120
That way, true balance can be achieved.

00:11:18.460 --> 00:11:19.240
Did you find that?

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.000
You mustn't do this.

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:23.160
The Village of Beginnings is irreplaceable.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.400
Yes, he's right.

00:11:24.680 --> 00:11:27.640
If you do this, just know that you're going to have to go through us first.

00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:29.360
Ooh, I'm trembling.

00:11:29.360 --> 00:11:29.840
Yo!

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:36.100
Well, I'd rather die than allow twisted sickos like you to destroy such a beautiful place.

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:38.260
They're tough, but we gotta stop them!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:40.350
We have to protect the eggs!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:41.560
I'm ready.

00:11:42.070 --> 00:11:43.230
Right behind you, buddy.

00:11:43.940 --> 00:11:44.400
Right.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.190
All right, then let's do it!

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:01.320
Show!

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:31.640
Haven't you two had enough already?

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:33.560
Better take cover, guys!

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:38.560
Bring it on!

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:47.420
How brave, yet ignorant!

00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:49.600
We don't intend to fight you, insects!

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:50.770
Say what?

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:53.320
We only came here to scan this village!

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:56.960
If you choose to get in the way, you will share the same fate!

00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:59.980
I suggest you and your little friends run along. We haven't-

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.510
an important mission to fulfill.

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:05.190
No, pal!

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:05.450
Huh?

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:06.970
Not on my watch!

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:09.000
Hold it!

00:13:09.510 --> 00:13:10.950
Where do you think you're going, Piggy?

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.210
Big mistake!

00:13:14.130 --> 00:13:15.550
You're insured...

00:13:15.550 --> 00:13:29.880
...to sacrifice our own lives to protect these eggs!

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:33.970
Shall I destroy you now, or would you like your humiliation prolonged?

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:36.330
Hey, why are they fighting back?

00:13:36.570 --> 00:13:38.850
Maybe they're afraid the eggs will be hurt if they fight here.

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:40.910
There's gotta be something we can do to help them.

00:13:41.070 --> 00:13:43.550
At least, I have this!

00:13:44.500 --> 00:13:46.040
You're right, they're not even trying.

00:13:46.220 --> 00:13:48.020
This place isn't safe for the eggs anymore.

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.380
The only way they'll survive is if we move them.

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:51.300
Good idea, Z.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:55.240
All right, people, we gotta do this fast and not let the knights see what we're doing.

00:13:56.030 --> 00:13:57.250
You are pathetic!

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.450
I think it's possible!

00:14:00.410 --> 00:14:01.430
Let them hurt the eggs.

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:03.310
That's a big, painful, duh.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.540
All right.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:07.760
Oh, dear.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:10.540
Keep going, guys.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.260
I'll hold them off as long as I can.

00:14:12.500 --> 00:14:13.780
We'll try to keep them distracted.

00:14:14.300 --> 00:14:16.480
We have to get these digi eggs out of here.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.120
I'm going to see the Traumon again.

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:18.720
Good luck.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.340
Village of Beginnings is under attack.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.980
We're collecting the digi eggs as fast as we can,

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:26.920
but we have no way of transporting them.

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:29.520
These are innocent little lives we're talking about.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:32.260
that they are the future of the digital world!

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:32.820
Please!

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:40.770
What is happening to this egg?

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:43.180
It's all pretty and glowing!

00:14:43.480 --> 00:14:45.400
What a crummy time to hatch!

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:46.620
That's not what they're doing!

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:57.100
Resistance is impressive,

00:14:57.420 --> 00:14:58.660
but I have a deadline!

00:14:59.020 --> 00:14:59.960
I'm afraid our...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.460
game is over. How can you be so callous about destroying a place like this? Have

00:15:04.460 --> 00:15:09.660
you no conscience? There is only one consciousness, that of Lord Lucianon. He

00:15:09.660 --> 00:15:14.040
alone has the power to restore order to the digital world. Yeah? Well it's obvious

00:15:14.040 --> 00:15:16.880
he's got some kind of power, at least enough to brainwash you dopes into

00:15:16.880 --> 00:15:22.580
believing that garbage. What? How dare you speak such blasphemy, you insignificant

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:23.480
worm!

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:33.620
What are we supposed to do now?

00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:04.880
Extra careful. I love babies.

00:16:06.170 --> 00:16:07.550
We can finish up here.

00:16:07.670 --> 00:16:09.610
The rest of you go help Takuya and Koji.

00:16:14.950 --> 00:16:17.390
Meddling mutants, you pay for that!

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:18.750
Say goodbye, little ones.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:20.630
You're about to become egg salad.

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:21.950
I don't think so.

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.200
You better back off right now.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:25.100
Or...

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:25.420
What?

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:42.920
Come on!

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:44.100
and ran him on!

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:45.570
Yeah, and Grumblemon?

00:16:45.960 --> 00:16:46.920
An Arbormon!

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:48.820
I can't believe it!

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.400
It looks like they've come to help.

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.980
What is this, a joke?!

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:56.020
We might be able to win if we combine the power of all ten warriors.

00:16:56.590 --> 00:16:57.570
They're all here!

00:16:57.810 --> 00:16:58.450
That's it!

00:16:58.790 --> 00:16:59.890
Let's put an end to this.

00:17:01.590 --> 00:17:01.850
Thank you.

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:11.620
together again!

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:13.830
Oh dear, I could just cry!

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:17.650
After everything we've been through, I never thought I'd live to see this day!

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.330
It's truly an historic moment in Digimon history!

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:23.990
Oh, I promised myself I wouldn't cry!

00:18:24.250 --> 00:18:24.770
Uh-huh!

00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:29.930
This can't be impossible!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.480
POSSIBLE!

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:32.220
Time to party!

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.580
Ah, Pyro!

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:34.830
Howling!

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:02.420
I'll try again another time.

00:19:02.580 --> 00:19:04.560
I'm not leaving without that village.

00:19:15.450 --> 00:19:15.970
Transmission!

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:24.460
It's gone. They've scanned it.

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:27.220
But every digi-egg is safely on board.

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:29.760
We couldn't have done it without the four of you.

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:30.650
cute

00:19:46.500 --> 00:19:47.540
about them being evil anymore.

00:19:48.490 --> 00:19:48.750
Huh?

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:52.110
I didn't think we'd see him again.

00:19:52.330 --> 00:19:54.150
Me either, but I'm glad we did.

00:19:54.890 --> 00:19:57.150
It all happened so fast, I never got to thank them.

00:19:57.360 --> 00:19:59.360
They look so happy, I don't think they even noticed.

00:20:00.020 --> 00:20:01.600
Seems like we all get to be reborn.

00:20:02.170 --> 00:20:02.970
whether we're people

00:20:03.420 --> 00:20:04.480
Or even Digimon!

00:20:05.110 --> 00:20:10.330
All aboard the Trailmont Express, he he he, keep the sunny side up!

00:20:10.840 --> 00:20:12.000
Funny, don't you know?

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.320
Egg-cellent job, guys!

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:18.020
Well, I'd sport these babies with loving care!

00:20:18.160 --> 00:20:20.940
Because we are the movers' egg-stra-ordinaire!

00:20:21.940 --> 00:20:23.320
These babies are going home.

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:25.980
And it's all thanks to you wonderful children.

00:20:26.380 --> 00:20:27.780
We should be thanking you.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:29.960
Now behave yourself, Pabu Monk!

00:20:32.550 --> 00:20:33.190
Do it!

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:39.660
I promise you guys, I'll never give up!

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:44.000
Until my friends and I have found a way to rebuild the digital world.

00:20:45.770 --> 00:20:46.370
seem to be back

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:49.300
But there's a lot of pieces missing.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:50.900
Let's see if they can put them back together

00:20:50.900 --> 00:20:53.300
on the next Digimon Digital Monsters.
